00:03:55.220 --> 00:04:01.420
A proper score is how it works when someone wants a private probability and can pay only after the event resolves.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:06.200
A strictly proper scoring rule makes honesty the strategic agent's best move.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.900
More accurate forecasts get higher scores in expectation.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.320
A 2018 paper on the archive takes that bargain as the baseline.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.540
Then asks what happens if the outcome never shows up and the principal has only the reports.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:25.440
Surrogate scoring rules add a bias correction and an error rate estimate for a reference answer

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.620
built from those reports.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:32.320
give the method one bit about the prior and run it across multiple tasks and

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.760
the paper says the surrogate recovers the strictly proper score in

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.820
expectation as if the ground truth were there. Quality can still be measured

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:45.600
without that ground truth. Dominant truthfulness in reporting comes along as a

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.760
by-product. The check was theoretical and it was also run on data from real human

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:57.240
forecasters. Multivariate questions are a different crack taken up in a 2015 monthly weather

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:03.640
review paper. Few proper scores exist for them, and many need a full density. The energy

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:09.500
score generalizes the continuous ranked probability score. That paper calls it the only commonly

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:15.820
used score that works on an ensemble, meaning a finite sample. It is weak at catching correlations

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.160
that were specified wrong.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.660
Various ground-based proper scores borrow a geostatistical idea.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:27.700
In simulations, they were more sensitive to bad means, bad variances, and bad correlations,

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.420
and sharper on the correlation structure itself.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:37.900
A case study of post-processed wind speed forecasts at five Colorado wind park sites showed the same pattern.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:43.760
A contract that pays when an event resolves is the setting where a proper rule can make honesty pay.

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:49.720
No ground truth or several correlated pieces in one question, and these papers say the score

